{
  "chapter": "foundations/nondeterminism",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "N samples of the same prompt. `agreementBps` is how often the most common answer",
    "appeared, in basis points, rounded with floor(x + 0.5).",
    "Ties on the modal answer break lexicographically, so the report is reproducible even",
    "when the model is not.",
    "`stable` is agreement at or above the consensus bar — it says nothing about correctness."
  ],
  "consensusBps": 8000,
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "identical-samples-are-stable",
      "samples": ["refund", "refund", "refund", "refund", "refund"],
      "result": { "modal": "refund", "modalCount": 5, "samples": 5, "agreementBps": 10000, "stable": true }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-bare-majority-is-not-consensus",
      "samples": ["refund", "refund", "refund", "escalate", "escalate"],
